WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.730
- Well, first concerts
provide indelible memories.

00:00:02.730 --> 00:00:04.300
You don't say indelible enough guys,

00:00:04.300 --> 00:00:05.880
memories for all of us.

00:00:05.880 --> 00:00:07.620
And just check this out.

00:00:07.620 --> 00:00:10.620
- I know we all have great
memories of our first concerts

00:00:10.620 --> 00:00:11.520
that we all went to.

00:00:11.520 --> 00:00:12.510
I know I do.

00:00:12.510 --> 00:00:14.520
- And my very first Heart
show was my first concert

00:00:14.520 --> 00:00:16.440
October 21st, 1978.

00:00:16.440 --> 00:00:19.680
- Puff Daddy, like not
P. Diddy, but Puff Daddy.

00:00:19.680 --> 00:00:20.513
- New Kids on the Block.

00:00:20.513 --> 00:00:21.568
- [Kelly] Oh, I gonna say a boy band.

00:00:21.568 --> 00:00:22.860
Okay, okay.
- At Dodger stadium.

00:00:22.860 --> 00:00:23.693
- Oh my gosh.

00:00:23.693 --> 00:00:24.526
- [Audience Member] Yeah.

00:00:24.526 --> 00:00:25.920
- I went to a Backstreet Boys concert

00:00:25.920 --> 00:00:27.330
and I threw up on the first song

00:00:27.330 --> 00:00:28.740
because the girls were so loud.

00:00:28.740 --> 00:00:29.700
They were screaming so loud.

00:00:29.700 --> 00:00:32.880
I don't know how that equaled
out to me throwing up, but.

00:00:32.880 --> 00:00:34.560
- It's overwhelming.
- I know it happened though.

00:00:34.560 --> 00:00:37.950
- I heard that your first ever
concert was pretty amazing.

00:00:37.950 --> 00:00:38.850
You wanna tell everybody who that was?

00:00:38.850 --> 00:00:40.080
- First ever?

00:00:40.080 --> 00:00:43.602
Oh, what a come around
moment with The Jackson 5.

00:00:43.602 --> 00:00:44.672
- [Kelly] That's amazing.

00:00:44.672 --> 00:00:45.712
- Yes.

00:00:45.712 --> 00:00:46.545
- [Kelly] Somebody told me that.

00:00:46.545 --> 00:00:47.760
Cause I always ask.

00:00:47.760 --> 00:00:48.900
Cause obviously I'm a musician.

00:00:48.900 --> 00:00:50.340
So I always ask like when people go see

00:00:50.340 --> 00:00:52.140
and that's your first concert?

00:00:52.140 --> 00:00:53.580
- Yes, had our little, you know,

00:00:53.580 --> 00:00:58.047
bolero jacket and hot pants
and Samson and Delilah sandals.

00:00:58.047 --> 00:00:58.880
(Kelly laughing)

00:00:58.880 --> 00:01:01.170
And I swear, they looked right at me

00:01:01.170 --> 00:01:03.240
and sang the song and it was just great.

00:01:03.240 --> 00:01:04.890
- Well, I just can't say it enough.

00:01:04.890 --> 00:01:06.906
It's a very rad first concert.

00:01:06.906 --> 00:01:08.430
(audience cheering)

00:01:08.430 --> 00:01:10.110
- Your dad of course is Phil Collins,

00:01:10.110 --> 00:01:12.170
which is incredible to
us and normal for you.

00:01:12.170 --> 00:01:13.003
(audience cheering)

00:01:13.003 --> 00:01:16.260
But it's just a really
cool thing for a musician.

00:01:16.260 --> 00:01:17.730
But what was your first concert?

00:01:17.730 --> 00:01:19.530
Like other than obviously your dad's.

00:01:19.530 --> 00:01:20.490
- The first concert I,

00:01:20.490 --> 00:01:21.900
it was NSYNC.

00:01:21.900 --> 00:01:22.733
- [Kelly] Oh my God.

00:01:22.733 --> 00:01:23.566
Did he get you like,

00:01:23.566 --> 00:01:24.600
did he hook you up?

00:01:24.600 --> 00:01:26.670
- [Lily] I, it was, it was a hookup,

00:01:26.670 --> 00:01:28.470
but it was really like, I just.

00:01:28.470 --> 00:01:30.570
- [Kelly] It's a hookup.
You're in a picture with them.

00:01:30.570 --> 00:01:32.190
Wait, I just saw the picture.

00:01:32.190 --> 00:01:33.180
They were babies.

00:01:33.180 --> 00:01:35.160
That's like one of their
first tours, maybe.

00:01:35.160 --> 00:01:36.420
- You know what was even crazier is

00:01:36.420 --> 00:01:37.500
you know who opened for them,

00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:39.390
that no one knew who she was?

00:01:39.390 --> 00:01:40.242
Britney Spears.

00:01:40.242 --> 00:01:41.075
- What?

00:01:41.075 --> 00:01:41.908
(audience gasping)

00:01:41.908 --> 00:01:42.960
- Your dad totally hooked you up.

00:01:42.960 --> 00:01:45.540
- Honest. He hooked, he
hooked up the opening act too.

00:01:45.540 --> 00:01:46.380
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:01:46.380 --> 00:01:47.940
- I remember sitting in the
audience and they were like

00:01:47.940 --> 00:01:49.770
oh, and please welcome the
opening act, Britney Spears.

00:01:49.770 --> 00:01:51.090
And everyone's like,

00:01:51.090 --> 00:01:52.770
who's, what, who's Britney Spears?

00:01:52.770 --> 00:01:54.720
And she came on and did
Hit Me Baby One More Time

00:01:54.720 --> 00:01:56.885
and everyone's like, well, she's good.

00:01:56.885 --> 00:01:58.068
(audience laughter)

00:01:58.068 --> 00:02:00.170
- She's good, she's gonna make it.

00:02:00.170 --> 00:02:01.003
- It was wild.

00:02:02.280 --> 00:02:04.980
- You were my first concert
I ever went to, in my life.

00:02:04.980 --> 00:02:05.880
- [Kelly] Oh, really?
- Yeah.

00:02:05.880 --> 00:02:07.290
- You were young.
- Yeah.

00:02:07.290 --> 00:02:08.123
- How old were you?

00:02:08.123 --> 00:02:09.390
- I had to be seven or eight,
- Oh wow.

00:02:09.390 --> 00:02:11.670
and it was me and my mom and my sisters.

00:02:11.670 --> 00:02:15.210
And I still have the
poster from your concert.

00:02:15.210 --> 00:02:16.110
It was,

00:02:16.110 --> 00:02:18.180
The Breakaway Days,
which I still listen to

00:02:18.180 --> 00:02:19.680
when I'm on airplanes and I cry.

00:02:19.680 --> 00:02:20.702
So it's great.

00:02:20.702 --> 00:02:21.684
(Kelly laughing)

00:02:21.684 --> 00:02:23.880
But yeah, you're just such
a, such an inspiration to me.

00:02:23.880 --> 00:02:24.963
- Oh, that's so kind.

00:02:26.616 --> 00:02:28.170
What were your first concerts,

00:02:28.170 --> 00:02:30.390
like your experience since
you love music so much?

00:02:30.390 --> 00:02:32.910
- My, my first concert, I
was invited to this concert

00:02:32.910 --> 00:02:34.369
of a band that I didn't know.

00:02:34.369 --> 00:02:35.202
- You already feel,

00:02:35.202 --> 00:02:37.770
you already feel like a loser?
- I'm apologizing for it.

00:02:37.770 --> 00:02:38.820
- But no, but it is like

00:02:38.820 --> 00:02:41.550
since you're asking my first concert,

00:02:41.550 --> 00:02:42.720
I was like, yeah sure I'll go.

00:02:42.720 --> 00:02:44.430
The band was The Hooters.

00:02:44.430 --> 00:02:45.263
Does it, do you remember this band?

00:02:45.263 --> 00:02:47.160
- Is it like the band for the restaurant?

00:02:47.160 --> 00:02:48.048
Like the wings?

00:02:48.048 --> 00:02:48.881
- No. No, no, no, no.

00:02:48.881 --> 00:02:49.714
Okay.

00:02:49.714 --> 00:02:50.640
Great, valid question.

00:02:50.640 --> 00:02:51.473
- [Kelly] Valid.

00:02:51.473 --> 00:02:52.650
- But they were like kind of,

00:02:52.650 --> 00:02:54.630
they had like a couple of hits

00:02:54.630 --> 00:02:56.700
in the late eighties, I think.

00:02:56.700 --> 00:02:57.840
- [Kelly] Oh. What was yours?

00:02:57.840 --> 00:03:00.090
- [Randall Park] My first
concert was very cool.

00:03:00.090 --> 00:03:00.930
- What was it?

00:03:00.930 --> 00:03:02.190
- I was a kid,
- Oh!

00:03:02.190 --> 00:03:03.930
but when Harry Met Sally had come out

00:03:03.930 --> 00:03:06.990
I was obsessed with that movie
and the music in the movie.

00:03:06.990 --> 00:03:09.450
- And Harry Connick Jr. did
a big part of the soundtrack.

00:03:09.450 --> 00:03:10.800
- He's great.
- Yeah.

00:03:10.800 --> 00:03:13.110
And I just, we would just
love the soundtrack so much.

00:03:13.110 --> 00:03:16.200
And me and a friend, found
out he was playing in Vegas.

00:03:16.200 --> 00:03:17.730
We, we grew up in L.A.

00:03:17.730 --> 00:03:20.787
And I begged my dad to, to
take us there, get us to

00:03:20.787 --> 00:03:22.596
- You begged your dad to take you?

00:03:22.596 --> 00:03:23.429
(Kelly laughing)

00:03:23.429 --> 00:03:26.490
- And he drove me and my friend to Vegas.

00:03:26.490 --> 00:03:27.360
And we just.

00:03:27.360 --> 00:03:29.490
- Your dad took you to
Vegas to see a show?

00:03:29.490 --> 00:03:30.323
- [Park] Yeah.

00:03:30.323 --> 00:03:31.156
- You have a cool dad.

00:03:31.156 --> 00:03:32.160
- Very cool of him, yeah.

00:03:32.160 --> 00:03:34.380
- Okay. Usually it's
like a pop band, like boy

00:03:34.380 --> 00:03:36.049
like its just like a
usually different scenario.

00:03:36.049 --> 00:03:36.882
- What are you saying,
what are you trying to say?

00:03:36.882 --> 00:03:38.460
- No, I just mean, usually
it was like, you were

00:03:38.460 --> 00:03:40.680
you had a very sophisticated
musical palette.

00:03:40.680 --> 00:03:42.146
- [Park] There you go, there you go.

00:03:42.146 --> 00:03:43.817
- Yeah, yeah, I got there, I got there.

00:03:43.817 --> 00:03:45.510
- How old were you?

00:03:45.510 --> 00:03:47.780
- Gosh, I must, maybe like
early high school maybe.

00:03:47.780 --> 00:03:49.650
- I just mean like, people would be like,

00:03:49.650 --> 00:03:51.060
can you take me to Janet Jackson?

00:03:51.060 --> 00:03:51.893
Can you take me?

00:03:51.893 --> 00:03:53.131
And you were like, please

00:03:53.131 --> 00:03:55.041
- Like, can you take me,
Harry, Harry Connick Jr.

00:03:55.041 --> 00:03:55.874
- He's amazing.
- And after that.

00:03:55.874 --> 00:03:58.080
- I just love him, as a
kid, it was different.

00:03:58.080 --> 00:04:00.184
- Like, can we go to the LA Phil?

00:04:00.184 --> 00:04:01.017
I really want,

00:04:01.017 --> 00:04:01.938
(Kelly and Park laughing)

00:04:01.938 --> 00:04:02.771
- Please, please.

00:04:02.771 --> 00:04:03.604
- [Ed Helms] They're
doing a Mozart special.

00:04:03.604 --> 00:04:06.395
- They are playing Vivaldi
Four Seasons and I must see it.

00:04:06.395 --> 00:04:08.093
- [Park] (laughs) I wanna
hear it, yeah, yeah.

